A||||6||LZeitgeist||Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show - Raleigh, NC||||1||
Z||000000||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||06:44 PM||||All right, where were you guys?!?! <P>Sat., Sept. 8th - Crown Pontiac in Raleigh NC - the Tarheel Tigers, a local GTO Owners Club held their First Annual All-Pontiac Car Show.<P>I showed up about 9:45 am to register the Formula, to find my Dad, Cal Heinske (and the Indy II) already there... John Miller (Formula88) was planning on meeting us there later. Dad decided not to enter the Indy II, because the interior is still too much of a work in progress, so I went up to Registration. <P>As I approached, the gentleman behind the table greeted me, and asked if he could help me... I asked him, smiling, "Hi! Are you guys a 'Fiero-friendly' club?" He said, "Sure! If it's got Pontiac on it, we love it!" I grinned and told him that I'd like to register my '88 Fiero Formula. That put me in Class 'M' - 1982 to Present Day, All Models. (The show had classes specifically for various year groupings of GTO-types, and year groupings for 1st- and 2nd-generation Firebirds. Class 'M' also included F-bodies (and anything else) Pontiac made from 1982 on... undaunted, I signed up anyway, knowing I'd be pitted against Firehawks, mid 80's and commemorative T/A's, and anything else that came in, but for a $15 entry fee, I figured I'd at least hopefully make a good impression and meet some new people.) <P>There was only one other Fiero entered - a silver 87 GT. I'm not sure why, but I noticed about 2:00 that he had left... he isn't online, so he didn't know about Pennock's or anything, so we talked for a while, and I told him about us here, but he said he works on computers a lot during the day, so he doesn't get online in the evenings.<P>Anyway, while judging was going on by members of the host club, a few well-versed volunteers, and a couple members of Crown Pontiac's sales force, we wandered and looked at the many, many, *many* fine (and a few perfectly pristine) examples of Pontiac's finest rolling stock (67 entries in all). About 3:00, they called us all up to begin handing out awards. <P>Lots of great cars won Class Awards - they didn't grant 1st, 2nd, 3rd etc. place standings - they picked the top three cars in most classes, and the top four in the 'M' class, due to a larger number of participants, and according to the judges, very hard choices having to be made.<P>I was *very* shocked to win one of the four awards given in the '82 to Present class! Whoohoo! <P>Pics below...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||06:45 PM||||   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow1">   <BR>Here's my baby on display...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow2">   <BR>Pic 1 of 3 of the majority of the '82 to Present lineup... red '95(?) T/A, my '88 Formula, a pair of '86(?) 2+2 MonteCarlo-esque Limited Editions, a 30th Anniversay T/A, and a *gorgeous 25th Anniversary Ram Air T/A - tweaked to match what the factory intended to do for that model to begin with.<BR>In the foregound are some of the LeMans & Tempests that were in attendance (but in their own class).<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow3">   <BR>Starting again from the left, a couple of black 2000 Ram Air T/As and a new Blaze(?) Orange Firehawk. Awesome...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow4">   <BR>From the left, a white Firebird Formula, red Ram Air T/A (damn, did they even *make* anything without Ram Air in the past couple years??), a very sweet black '86 T/A T-top, another black Ram Air T/A, and another white Firebird Formula.<BR>In the foreground, a matching Firehawk to the one in the previous picture, and a couple more LeMans...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow5">   <BR>Here was half the lineup in the upper lot - lots of 1st- and 2nd-gen Firebirds in this line, including a '69 and a '71 that John drooled over until he had to be escorted away &lt;g&gt;, and a Bandit Replica that caught my eye more than once...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow6">   <BR>They even had a few entries from the golden age of Pontiac... when the logo was the Big Chief instead of the arrowhead we know today... <P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagekronos/RaleighShow7">   <BR>There's my baby, looking as sweet and fine as the brand-new models right next to her... yummy.<P><BR>-----------------<P>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - '1982 to Present' - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||09-08-2001||10:50 PM||||Congrats Patrick!<P>I had family visiting this weekend so I couldn't make the drive over today.  I haven't had any time to get the blue GT cleaned up since the trip back from AL last week.  <P>See you at our meeting in October in Raleigh!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||11:07 PM||||Thanks, Bob... sorry you missed it - *lots* of great-looking rolling eye-candy...<P>It's a really great group of people, too.||||reg||1
